      "final_text": "Done. `lake build Solution` passes with all five theorems proved and no `sorry`.\n\nWhat changed (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean), 925 lines):\n\n- `sqrt` is now the deployed loop with the PR-4486 choice: `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)`. On the issue input the loop ends at `(9999999998, 9999999999)` and the old code returned the second (above the root); the minimum returns the floor.\n- The proof mirrors the loop on `Nat` (`fstep`, `nloop`, `zseq`) and shows the minimum of the final iterates equals `Nat.sqrt (a*10^10)`: lower bound `f(z) \u2265 S` via `(z-S)^2 \u2265 0`, halving `f(z)-S \u2264 (z-S)/2` above `S`, fixed-point analysis (`f(S+1) = S`, fixed points are `S`), and a capped-excess induction showing 255 steps settle both final iterates into `{S, S+1}`. Range checks (`q+z \u2264 2^167-1`) come from a crude `S < 2^101` bound plus the seed bound `S \u2264 a/2+5\u00b710^9` (AM-GM over `Int`).\n- `req_deployed_loop` and `req_sqrt_neg_reverts` hold by definition; `req_sqrt_total`, `req_sqrt_not_above`, `req_sqrt_not_below` follow from the main lemma `sqrt_some_floor` plus `Nat.sqrt_le` / `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`.\n\nVerification observed: clean `lake build Solution` (only unused-variable/simp warnings); `#print axioms` gives exactly `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` for the three arithmetic theorems and none for the rest; grep confirms no forbidden tokens and only allowed imports; all locked-file hashes match [locked.json](<workspace>/spec/locked.json); scratch files removed. One note: a direct `decide` evaluation of `sqrt 9999999998` still hits the kernel recursion limit, so point-wise execution wasn't re-checked in Lean \u2014 the floor property for that input follows from the proved theorems instead.",
